    (596, "Epinephrine Adrenergic Receptors: Alpha-1, Beta-1, and Beta-2 Pathways", "Alpha-1 (Gq -> PLC -> IP3/Ca2+ vasoconstriction); Beta-1 (Gs -> heart rate/contractility); Beta-2 (Gs -> bronchial/vascular smooth muscle dilation, glycogenolysis)."),
    (597, "Cortisol Glucocorticoid Receptor Signaling & Hepatic Gluconeogenesis", "Intracellular nuclear receptor binding; homodimerization, nuclear translocation, binding GREs, transcribing PEPCK and glucose-6-phosphatase genes."),
    (598, "Thyroid Hormone (T3/T4) Genomic Activation of Na+/K+-ATPase", "T3 binding nuclear thyroid receptors; upregulating transcription of Na+/K+-ATPase and uncoupling proteins; elevating basal metabolic rate and oxygen consumption."),
    (599, "Growth Hormone & Insulin-Like Growth Factor-1 (IGF-1) Anabolic Axis", "Anterior pituitary GH stimulating hepatic secretion of IGF-1; promotes chondrocyte proliferation, skeletal elongation, and amino acid uptake."),
    (600, "Sphingolipid Metabolism: Sphingomyelin, Cerebrosides, and Gangliosides", "Ceramide backbone (sphingosine + fatty acid); sphingomyelin in myelin sheath; cerebrosides (neutral monosaccharide); gangliosides (acidic sialic acid NANA)."),
    (601, "Lysosomal Sphingolipidoses: Tay-Sachs Disease (Hexosaminidase A)", "Deficiency of Hexosaminidase A causing GM2 ganglioside accumulation in neurons; developmental regression, cherry-red macular spot, exaggerated startle, no hepatomegaly."),
    (602, "Lysosomal Sphingolipidoses: Gaucher Disease (Glucocerebrosidase)", "Most common lysosomal storage disease; glucocerebroside accumulation in macrophages ('crumpled tissue paper' histiocytes); hepatosplenomegaly, bone crises."),
    (603, "Lysosomal Sphingolipidoses: Niemann-Pick Disease (Sphingomyelinase)", "Sphingomyelinase deficiency causing sphingomyelin accumulation; foam cells, hepatosplenomegaly, neurodegeneration, cherry-red spot on macula."),
    (604, "Lysosomal Sphingolipidoses: Fabry Disease (Alpha-Galactosidase A)", "X-linked recessive; globotriaosylceramide (Gb3) accumulation; peripheral burning neuropathy (acroparesthesias), angiokeratomas, progressive renal failure."),
    (605, "Eicosanoid Biosynthesis: Phospholipase A2, Cyclooxygenases (COX-1/2), and Lipoxygenase", "Membrane phospholipids cleaved by PLA2 to release arachidonic acid; COX-1/2 generating prostaglandins/thromboxane; 5-LOX generating leukotrienes."),

    # D. Molecular Biology, Genetics, DNA Replication & Repair (606 - 650)
    (606, "Eukaryotic Replication Fork: Pol alpha, Pol delta, Pol epsilon & PCNA", "Pol alpha/primase synthesizes RNA/DNA primer; Pol epsilon synthesizes leading strand; Pol delta synthesizes lagging strand Okazaki fragments with PCNA sliding clamp."),
    (607, "DNA Topoisomerase I and II (Gyrase) Mechanisms & Inhibitors", "Topoisomerase I (single-strand nick, campothecin target); Topoisomerase II (double-strand cut, etoposide/doxorubicin and bacterial ciprofloxacin targets)."),
    (608, "Telomere Maintenance, T-Loop Structure & Shelterin Complex", "TTAGGG tandem hexanucleotide repeats; 3' single-stranded overhang invading double strand forming protective t-loop capped by shelterin protein complex."),
    (609, "Telomerase Reverse Transcriptase (TERT) & Human Cellular Senescence", "Ribonucleoprotein enzyme containing internal RNA template (TERC); highly active in germ cells and > 90% of malignant cancers; inactive in somatic tissues."),
    (610, "DNA Mismatch Repair (MMR) & Lynch Syndrome / HNPCC Genetics", "MutS/MutL homolog heterodimers (MSH2, MSH6, MLH1, PMS2) recognizing base mismatches and insertion/deletion loops; microsatellite instability (MSI)."),
    (611, "Base Excision Repair (BER): DNA Glycosylases & AP Endonuclease", "Specific DNA glycosylase cleaving N-glycosidic bond of oxidized or deaminated base (uracil-DNA glycosylase); AP endonuclease cleaving 5' phosphodiester bond."),
    (612, "Double-Strand Break Repair: Homologous Recombination (HR) & BRCA1/BRCA2", "Error-free S/G2 repair utilizing sister chromatid template; MRN complex resection (3' overhangs), Rad51 recombinase strand invasion; synthetic lethality with PARP inhibitors."),
    (613, "Double-Strand Break Repair: Non-Homologous End Joining (NHEJ) & Ku70/80", "Ku70/80 heterodimer binding broken DNA ends, recruiting DNA-PKcs and Artemis endonuclease; error-prone direct ligation by Ligase IV-XRCC4; causes deletions/translocations."),
    (614, "Chemical DNA Mutagens: Alkylating Agents & Cross-Linking Nitrogen Mustards", "O6-methylguanine mispairing with thymine during replication; bifunctional alkylating agents (cyclophosphamide) forming interstrand covalent cross-links."),
    (615, "Somatic vs Germline Mutations & Evolutionary Heritability", "Somatic mutations confined to individual tissues (drives carcinogenesis, cannot be inherited); germline mutations present in gametes, transmitted to all offspring cells."),
    (616, "Mendelian Autosomal Dominant Inheritance & Achondroplasia", "Heterozygotes affected; 50% recurrence risk per pregnancy; vertical pedigree transmission; FGFR3 gain-of-function mutation; incomplete penetrance and variable expressivity."),
    (617, "Mendelian Autosomal Recessive Inheritance & Cystic Fibrosis (CFTR)", "Horizontal pedigree pattern (affected siblings with normal parents); 25% recurrence risk; CFTR delta-F508 misfolding mutation; carrier screening."),
    (618, "X-Linked Recessive Inheritance: Hemophilia A & Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy", "Males predominantly affected; no male-to-male transmission; carrier mothers transmitting mutant allele to 50% of sons; skewed lyonization in females."),
    (619, "X-Linked Dominant Inheritance: Fragile X & Rett Syndrome", "Affected fathers transmitting trait to 100% of daughters and 0% of sons; affected mothers transmitting to 50% of offspring; trinucleotide CGG repeats."),
    (620, "Mitochondrial Maternal Inheritance & Heteroplasmy", "Transmitted exclusively through oocyte cytoplasm; mother transmits to all children; variable phenotypic severity depending on threshold proportion of mutant mtDNA (heteroplasmy)."),
    (621, "Genetic Penetrance vs Expressivity in Human Disease", "Penetrance (percentage of individuals with genotype who exhibit the clinical phenotype); Expressivity (severity or spectrum of symptoms among individuals with same genotype)."),
    (622, "Genetic Linkage & Recombination Frequency (Centimorgans / Map Units)", "Genes located close together on same chromosome violating independent assortment; 1% recombination frequency = 1 map unit (cM); max recombination = 50%."),
    (623, "Eukaryotic Pre-mRNA Splicing: Spliceosome Assembly & Lariat Intermediate", "U1 snRNP binding 5' splice site (GU), U2 snRNP binding branch point adenosine, U4/U6/U5 tri-snRNP; 2'-5' phosphodiester bond forming intron lariat."),
    (624, "Alternative Splicing: Exon Skipping & Mutual Exclusion", "Single pre-mRNA primary transcript spliced into multiple distinct mature mRNA isoforms; expanded proteomic diversity (e.g., muscle vs non-muscle tropomyosin)."),
    (625, "RNA Editing: Apolipoprotein B-100 vs B-48 Cytidine Deamination", "APOBEC-1 cytidine deaminase in intestine deaminating CAA (Gln) to UAA (stop codon), truncating full-length ApoB-100 into ApoB-48 chylomicron protein."),
    (626, "The Genetic Code: Wobble Hypothesis & Inosine Base-Pairing", "Non-standard Watson-Crick base-pairing at 3rd base of codon (5' base of tRNA anticodon); inosine base-pairing with A, U, or C; explains degeneracy."),
    (627, "Aminoacyl-tRNA Synthetase Fidelity & The Double-Sieve Proofreading Mechanism", "Activation site selecting amino acids by size/charge; hydrolytic editing pocket hydrolyzing misactivated smaller amino acids (e.g., valine misactivated by isoleucyl-tRNA synthetase)."),
    (628, "Prokaryotic Ribosome Structure: 70S (50S + 30S) & Antibiotic Targets", "Aminoglycosides binding 30S A-site causing misreading; Tetracycline blocking aminoacyl-tRNA binding to A-site; Chloramphenicol inhibiting 50S peptidyl transferase."),
    (629, "Eukaryotic Ribosome Structure: 80S (60S + 40S) & Ribosomal Toxins", "Ricin (castor bean) depurinating a single conserved adenine in 28S rRNA; Diphtheria toxin ADP-ribosylating eukaryotic elongation factor-2 (eEF-2), halting translation."),
    (630, "Translational Control: Eukaryotic Initiation Factor-2 (eIF-2) Phosphorylation", "Cellular stress kinases (PERK, PKR) phosphorylating eIF-2alpha, sequestering eIF-2B guanine nucleotide exchange factor, shutting down global protein synthesis."),
    (631, "The Trp Operon: Transcriptional Attenuation Mechanism", "High tryptophan levels allow rapid translation of leader peptide, forming 3-4 transcription terminator hairpin; low tryptophan stalls ribosome at Trp codons, forming 2-3 anti-terminator."),
    (632, "Chromatin Remodeling: Histone Deacetylases (HDACs) & Transcriptional Repression", "HDACs removing acetyl groups, restoring positive charges on lysine residues, condensing chromatin into transcriptionally silent heterochromatin."),
    (633, "DNA Methylation: DNA Methyltransferases (DNMT1 vs DNMT3A/3B)", "DNMT3A/3B establishing de novo methylation on cytosines in CpG islands; DNMT1 maintaining methylation patterns across replication; recruiting methyl-CpG binding proteins (MeCP2)."),
    (634, "Genomic Imprinting: Epigenetic Parent-of-Origin Expression", "Differential methylation during gametogenesis; Prader-Willi syndrome (deletion of paternal 15q11-q13) vs Angelman syndrome (deletion of maternal 15q11-q13)."),
    (635, "X-Chromosome Inactivation (Lyonization) & The Xist lncRNA", "Random transcriptional silencing of one X chromosome in female mammalian blastocysts; Xist long non-coding RNA coating inactive X, recruiting polycomb repressive complexes (Barr body)."),
    (636, "Enhancer Loops & Mediator Complex in Eukaryotic Transcription", "Distal enhancer-bound transcription factors looping long chromosomal distances to interact with the core promoter via the multi-protein Mediator complex."),
    (637, "Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR): Primers, Taq Polymerase & Thermal Cycles", "Denaturation (95 °C), Primer Annealing (55-65 °C based on Tm), Primer Extension (72 °C); 2^n exponential amplification; designing forward and reverse primers."),
    (638, "Quantitative Real-Time PCR (RT-qPCR) & The 2^(-DeltaDeltaCt) Method", "SYBR Green intercalating dye vs TaqMan fluorogenic probes; threshold cycle (Ct) inversely proportional to initial template copy number; quantifying relative gene expression."),
    (639, "Recombinant DNA Technology: Restriction Endonucleases & Plasmids", "Type II restriction endonucleases recognizing palindromic recognition sequences; sticky ends vs blunt ends; plasmid cloning vectors (origin, multiple cloning site, selectable antibiotic marker)."),
    (640, "DNA Sanger Dideoxy Sequencing vs Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS)", "Dideoxynucleoside triphosphates (ddNTPs) lacking 3'-OH terminating chain synthesis; NGS sequencing-by-synthesis parallel flow cells yielding gigabases of data."),
    (641, "Southern Blotting vs Northern Blotting vs Western Blotting", "Southern (gel electrophoresis and probe hybridization for DNA); Northern (evaluating RNA transcript size and abundance); Western (antibody detection of specific proteins)."),
    (642, "Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay (ELISA): Direct vs Indirect vs Sandwich", "Direct (labeled primary antibody); Indirect (unlabeled primary + labeled secondary antibody); Sandwich (capture antibody on plate, antigen, detection antibody; high sensitivity)."),
    (643, "Chromatin Immunoprecipitation (ChIP): Mapping In Vivo Transcription Factor Binding", "Formaldehyde cross-linking protein to DNA in living cells, sonication to shear chromatin, immunoprecipitation with specific antibody, uncoupling, and PCR sequencing (ChIP-seq)."),
    (644, "Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH) in Clinical Cytogenetics", "Fluorophore-labeled DNA probes hybridized directly to fixed metaphase chromosomes or interphase nuclei; detecting chromosomal microdeletions, translocations (BCR-ABL)."),
    (645, "Recombinant Protein Expression in E. coli: Inclusion Bodies & Chaperones", "High-level expression driven by T7 RNA polymerase/IPTG induction; misfolded insoluble inclusion bodies requiring denaturing extraction and in vitro refolding."),
    (646, "Gene Knockout Technologies: Homologous Recombination vs Cre-LoxP Conditional Knockouts", "Conventional germline knockout vs Cre recombinase excising DNA flanked by loxP sites in a cell-type-specific or temporally controlled manner."),
    (647, "Transgenic Organisms: Pronuclear Microinjection vs Viral Transduction", "Microinjecting foreign recombinant DNA directly into the male pronucleus of a fertilized zygote; random genomic integration and mosaic expression."),
    (648, "RNA Sequencing (RNA-seq) & The Cellular Transcriptome", "Total RNA extraction, ribosomal RNA depletion, reverse transcription to cDNA library, high-throughput sequencing, alignment to reference genome to quantify splice variants."),
    (649, "Microarray Hybridization for Global Gene Expression Profiling", "Microscopic silicon chips spotted with thousands of single-stranded oligonucleotide probes; dual-color competitive cDNA hybridization (tumor vs normal)."),
    (650, "Flow Cytometry & Fluorescence-Activated Cell Sorting (FACS)", "Hydrodynamic focusing of cells in single file past laser beams; forward scatter (size), side scatter (granularity), multi-color fluorophore antibody sorting into viable pools."),
    # Additional B/B Topics (651 - 740)
    # E. Cell Biology, Organelles, Membrane Transport & Microbiology (651 - 695)
    (651, "Eukaryotic Plasma Membrane: Lipid Rafts & Bilayer Asymmetry", "Cholesterol buffering membrane fluidity, sphingolipids, GPI anchors, ATP-dependent flippases/floppases/scramblases maintaining asymmetric inner/outer leaflet composition."),
    (652, "Simple Diffusion, Osmosis & Aquaporin Water Channels", "Fick's first law of diffusion, osmotic pressure van 't Hoff equation (Pi = iMRT), aquaporin NPA motifs preventing proton conductance across cell membranes."),
    (653, "Facilitated Diffusion: GLUT Transporters & Ion Channels", "Carrier vs channel-mediated passive transport, GLUT1 basal vs GLUT4 insulin-dependent vesicle translocation, patch-clamp recordings of single-channel currents."),
    (654, "Primary Active Transport: Na+/K+-ATPase & Ca2+-ATPase (SERCA)", "P-type ATPases, E1/E2 conformational states, cardiotonic steroids (ouabain, digoxin) inhibiting Na+/K+ pump, thapsigargin SERCA blockade elevating cytosolic Ca2+."),
    (655, "Secondary Active Transport: Symporters (Cotransporters) & Antiporters", "Na+/glucose SGLT1 cotransport, Na+/Ca2+ NCX exchanger stoichiometry, electroneutral vs electrogenic coupled transport driven by electrochemical ion gradients."),
    (656, "Endocytosis: Clathrin-Coated Pits, Caveolae & Pinocytosis", "Receptor-mediated endocytosis of LDL, dynamin GTPase vesicle pinching, caveolin oligomers in lipid rafts, non-specific macropinocytosis fluid engulfment."),
    (657, "Exocytosis & Vesicle Fusion: SNARE Hypothesis & Synaptotagmin", "v-SNARE synaptobrevin pairing with t-SNARE syntaxin/SNAP-25 four-helix bundle, Ca2+ sensor synaptotagmin, botulinum/tetanus neurotoxin endopeptidase cleavage."),
    (658, "Nuclear Envelope, Nuclear Pore Complexes & Nucleocytoplasmic Transport", "Nuclear pore FG nucleoporin repeats, importin-alpha/beta cargo binding, Ran-GTP/Ran-GDP asymmetric gradient driving directional nuclear import and export."),
    (659, "Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum: Signal Peptide Recognition & Translocation", "N-terminal hydrophobic signal peptide, signal recognition particle (SRP) GTPase binding, Sec61 translocon channel docking, lumenal signal peptidase cleavage."),
    (660, "Protein N-Glycosylation & Quality Control in the ER Lumen", "Dolichol pyrophosphate oligosaccharide precursor transfer, calnexin/calreticulin chaperone folding, ER-associated degradation (ERAD) via retrotranslocation to ubiquitin-proteasome."),
    (661, "Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum: Lipid Synthesis & Xenobiotic Detoxification", "Phospholipid/cholesterol synthesis, cytochrome P450 monooxygenase hydroxylation of lipophilic toxins, specialized sarcoplasmic reticulum intracellular Ca2+ sequestration."),
    (662, "Golgi Apparatus: Cis/Medial/Trans Cisternae & Vesicular Trafficking", "COPI retrograde transport to ER, COPII anterograde transport from ER, O-linked glycosylation on Ser/Thr, mannose-6-phosphate tagging for lysosomal enzyme targeting."),
    (663, "Lysosomes, Acid Hydrolases & Sphingolipidoses", "Vacuolar V-ATPase proton pump maintaining acidic lumen (pH 4.5-5.0), glucocerebrosidase deficiency (Gaucher disease), hexosaminidase A deficiency (Tay-Sachs disease), LC3-mediated autophagy."),
    (664, "Peroxisomes: Very Long-Chain Fatty Acid (VLCFA) Oxidation & Catalase", "Peroxin biogenesis proteins (Zellweger spectrum), alpha-oxidation of branched-chain phytanic acid (Refsum disease), hydrogen peroxide (H2O2) generation and catalase decomposition."),
    (665, "Mitochondria: Double Membrane, Cristae & Mitochondrial Genetics", "Porin-permeable outer membrane, cardiolipin-rich impermeable inner membrane, maternal cytoplasmic inheritance of circular mtDNA, heteroplasmy threshold effect."),
    (666, "Cytoskeleton Microfilaments: Actin Dynamics, Treadmilling & Myosin", "G-actin to F-actin ATP-dependent polymerization, critical concentration (Cc), barbed (+) vs pointed (-) ends, treadmilling equilibrium, cytochalasin vs phalloidin toxin mechanisms."),
    (667, "Cytoskeleton Intermediate Filaments: Keratin, Vimentin, Desmin & Lamins", "Non-polar rope-like tensile tetramers, desmosomal structural integrity in epithelial sheets, nuclear lamina phosphorylation and disassembly during mitotic prophase."),
    (668, "Cytoskeleton Microtubules: Tubulin Heterodimers & Dynamic Instability", "GTP cap hydrolysis, catastrophe vs rescue transitions, kinesin anterograde (+) vs dynein retrograde (-) motor transport, paclitaxel microtubule stabilization vs colchicine depolymerization."),
    (669, "Centrosomes, Centrioles & Microtubule Organizing Centers (MTOCs)", "9+0 triplet microtubule centriole architecture, gamma-tubulin ring complexes (gamma-TuRC) nucleating spindle microtubules, pericentriolar material duplication during S phase."),
    (670, "Cilia and Flagella Ultrastructure: The 9+2 Axoneme & Dynein Arms", "Radial spokes, nexin elastic links, axonemal dynein ATPase arms driving doublet microtubule sliding and ciliary bending, primary ciliary dyskinesia (Kartagener syndrome)."),
    (671, "Cell Junctions: Tight Junctions (Zonula Occludens) & Epithelial Polarity", "Claudin and occludin transmembrane strands, blood-brain barrier and intestinal epithelial barrier sealing, apicobasal polarity maintenance, transepithelial electrical resistance."),
    (672, "Cell Junctions: Adherens Junctions & Desmosomes (Anchoring Junctions)", "Cadherin homophilic Ca2+-dependent extracellular adhesion, catenin linkage to actin filaments; desmogleins/desmocollins linked to intermediate filaments, pemphigus vulgaris autoantibodies."),
    (673, "Cell Junctions: Gap Junctions & Intercellular Metabolic Coupling", "Connexin hexamers forming transmembrane connexon channels, passive intercellular diffusion of inorganic ions and second messengers (<1 kDa), cardiac intercalated disc synchronization."),
    (674, "Extracellular Matrix (ECM): Collagen, Elastin, Fibronectin & Integrins", "Triple-helix procollagen synthesis and vitamin C-dependent proline hydroxylation, tropoelastin cross-linking, fibronectin RGD motif, heterodimeric integrin focal adhesions."),
    (675, "Cell Cycle Phases: Interphase (G1, S, G2) & Cyclin-CDK Regulation", "Cyclin D-CDK4/6 phosphorylating retinoblastoma protein (pRb), E2F release, Cyclin E-CDK2 firing G1/S transition, Cyclin B-CDK1 (MPF) driving mitotic entry."),
    (676, "Cell Cycle Checkpoints: G1/S, G2/M & Spindle Assembly Checkpoint (SAC)", "ATM/ATR kinase DNA break detection, p53 stabilization, p21 CIP1/WAF1 CDK inhibition, Mad2 kinetochore tension sensing inhibiting APC/C until amphitelic attachment."),
    (677, "Mitosis: Prophase, Metaphase, Anaphase & Telophase Mechanics", "Chromosome condensation (condensin), kinetochore microtubule capture, APC/C-mediated securin degradation, separase cleaving cohesin rings, cytokinesis actomyosin contractile ring."),
    (678, "Apoptosis: Intrinsic (Mitochondrial) vs Extrinsic (Death Receptor) Pathways", "Bax/Bak pore formation, cytochrome c release, Apaf-1 apoptosome assembly, procaspase-9 cleavage vs FasL/TNF death receptor DISC activation of initiator caspase-8/10."),
    (679, "Cancer Biology: Oncogenes, Tumor Suppressor Genes & The Hallmarks of Cancer", "Constitutively active Ras GTPase, Myc amplification, Knudson's two-hit loss of Rb/TP53, telomerase TERT reactivation, VEGF angiogenic switch, epithelial-mesenchymal transition (EMT)."),
    (680, "Stem Cells: Totipotency, Pluripotency, Multipotency & Differentiation", "Morula blastomeres (totipotent), blastocyst inner cell mass (pluripotent, Oct4/Sox2/Nanog), adult hematopoietic stem cells (multipotent), asymmetric self-renewing division."),
    (681, "Bacterial Cell Envelope: Gram-Positive vs Gram-Negative Architecture", "Thick peptidoglycan with lipoteichoic acids vs thin peptidoglycan with asymmetric outer membrane, LPS endotoxin lipid A, periplasmic space beta-lactamase retention."),
    (682, "Bacterial Motility: Flagellar Motor & Chemotactic Signal Transduction", "Basal body rotor embedded in cell envelope driven by proton motive force (PMF), counterclockwise run vs clockwise tumble, CheA histidine kinase and CheY response regulator phosphorylation."),
    (683, "Bacterial Growth Kinetics: Lag, Exponential, Stationary & Death Phases", "Binary fission generation time doubling equation (N = N0 * 2^n), nutrient limitation, secondary metabolite and endospore formation in stationary phase, viable but non-culturable state."),
    (684, "Bacterial Genetic Recombination: Transformation, Transduction & Conjugation", "Natural competence exogenous DNA uptake, generalized vs specialized bacteriophage transduction, F-plasmid sex pilus and high-frequency recombination (Hfr) chromosomal transfer."),
    (685, "Bacterial Transposons & Antibiotic Resistance Dissemination", "Insertion sequences, composite transposons carrying aminoglycoside or beta-lactamase genes, integrons and horizontal gene transfer via multidrug resistance plasmids."),
    (686, "Viral Structure: Capsid Symmetry, Enveloped vs Non-Enveloped Viruses", "Icosahedral vs helical capsomer geometry, host-derived lipid envelope susceptibility to detergents/heat, non-enveloped viral environmental stability, viral attachment glycoproteins."),
    (687, "Viral Classification: Baltimore Classification Scheme (Groups I - VII)", "dsDNA (I), ssDNA (II), dsRNA (III), positive-sense ssRNA (IV, directly infectious mRNA), negative-sense ssRNA (V, packaging RNA-dependent RNA polymerase), ssRNA-RT (VI), dsDNA-RT (VII)."),
    (688, "Bacteriophage Life Cycles: Lytic vs Lysogenic Phages & Prophage Induction", "Immediate virulent viral burst vs temperate lambda prophage integration into host bacterial genome, CI repressor maintaining lysogeny vs Cro transcriptional switch upon UV damage."),
    (689, "Retroviruses: Reverse Transcriptase, Integrase & The HIV Replication Cycle", "Dimeric (+)ssRNA reverse transcription to proviral dsDNA, lack of proofreading error rate, integrase nuclear targeting, Gag/Pol/Env polyprotein processing by viral protease."),
    (690, "Subviral Pathogens: Prions & Pathological Amyloid Conformational Cascades", "PrP^C alpha-helical native monomer template-directed refolding into insoluble beta-sheet-rich PrP^Sc fibrils, resistance to autoclaving and proteases, spongiform encephalopathy."),
    (691, "Subviral Pathogens: Viroids & Plant Pathogenesis Mechanisms", "Small circular single-stranded non-coding RNA molecules lacking protein capsids, autonomous rolling-circle replication via host RNA polymerase II, catalytic hammerhead ribozyme self-cleavage."),
    (692, "Cellular Senescence, The Hayflick Limit & Telomere Shortening", "Replicative arrest after ~50 population doublings, uncapped telomere persistent DNA damage response, Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype (SASP) pro-inflammatory cytokines."),
    (693, "Autophagy & Organellar Turnover: Mitophagy & Proteostasis", "PINK1 kinase accumulation on depolarized mitochondrial outer membrane, Parkin E3 ubiquitin ligase recruitment, p62/SQSTM1 adaptor binding to LC3-II autophagosomal membranes."),
    (694, "Microbial Culture Techniques: Selective, Differential & Enrichment Media", "MacConkey agar (bile salts/crystal violet inhibiting Gram-positives; neutral red lactose fermentation indicator), blood agar (alpha/beta/gamma hemolysis patterns), mannitol salt agar."),
    (695, "Innate Host Cellular Defenses: Interferon-Stimulated Genes (ISGs)", "Viral dsRNA sensing by TLR3/RIG-I, Type I IFN-alpha/beta autocrine/paracrine signaling via JAK-STAT, 2'-5'-oligoadenylate synthetase (OAS) activating RNase L, PKR translation shutdown."),
    # F. Organ Systems Physiology & Integrative Biology (696 - 740)
    (696, "Central Nervous System: Cerebral Cortex, Basal Ganglia & Diencephalon", "Frontal, parietal, temporal, and occipital functional specializations; basal ganglia direct (movement-promoting) vs indirect (movement-inhibiting) pathways; thalamus and hypothalamus."),
    (697, "Peripheral Nervous System: Somatic vs Autonomic Sympathetic & Parasympathetic", "Two-neuron autonomic circuits: thoracolumbar sympathetic (short preganglionic ACh, long postganglionic NE) vs craniosacral parasympathetic (long preganglionic ACh, short postganglionic ACh)."),
    (698, "Reflex Arcs: Monosynaptic Stretch vs Polysynaptic Flexor-Withdrawal Reflexes", "Muscle spindle Ia afferents directly synapsing onto alpha-motoneurons (patellar stretch), Golgi tendon organ Ib reciprocal inhibition, flexor withdrawal with crossed extensor reflex."),
    (699, "Synaptic Transmission: Voltage-Gated Ca2+ Channels & Postsynaptic Potentials", "Pre-synaptic N/P/Q-type voltage-gated Ca2+ influx triggering vesicular exocytosis, ionotropic ligand-gated receptors generating fast EPSPs/IPSPs vs slow GPCR metabotropic modulations."),
    (700, "Neurotransmitter Homeostasis: Synthesis, Reuptake Transporters & Catabolism", "Choline acetyltransferase and acetylcholinesterase; tyrosine hydroxylase catecholamine pathway, monoamine oxidase (MAO) and catechol-O-methyltransferase (COMT); glutamate-glutamine cycle."),
    (701, "Endocrine Signaling: Peptide, Steroid & Tyrosine-Derived Hormone Classes", "Hydrophilic peptide hormones (insulin, PTH) binding plasma membrane GPCRs/RTKs; hydrophobic steroid hormones (cortisol, estrogen) binding cytosolic/nuclear receptors; thyroid hormones vs catecholamines."),
    (702, "Hypothalamic-Anterior Pituitary Portal System & Neuroendocrine Axes", "Hypophyseal portal system transport of releasing hormones: GnRH -> LH/FSH, GHRH -> GH, TRH -> TSH, CRH -> ACTH, dopamine tonic inhibition of prolactin secretion."),
    (703, "Posterior Pituitary Neurohormones: Oxytocin & Arginine Vasopressin (ADH)", "Synthesized in magnocellular neurosecretory cells of supraoptic and paraventricular nuclei, transported along hypothalamic-hypophyseal tract; oxytocin milk ejection, ADH V2 aquaporin-2 water reabsorption."),
    (704, "Thyroid Hormone Synthesis, Transport & Basal Metabolic Rate Regulation", "Thyroid follicular iodide trapping via NIS symporter, thyroperoxidase (TPO) iodination of thyroglobulin, pinocytosis, peripheral conversion of T4 to active T3 by 5'-deiodinase, genomic thermogenesis."),
    (705, "Calcium & Phosphate Mineral Homeostasis: PTH, Calcitriol & Calcitonin", "Chief cell CaSR sensing low extracellular Ca2+, parathyroid hormone (PTH) stimulating osteoclast resorption and renal 1-alpha-hydroxylase producing 1,25-(OH)2D3; calcitonin opposing bone resorption."),
    (706, "Adrenal Physiology: Cortical Zonation (GFR) & Medullary Catecholamines", "Zona glomerulosa (aldosterone), zona fasciculata (cortisol), zona reticularis (DHEA androgens); adrenal medulla chromaffin cells secreting epinephrine and norepinephrine under sympathetic control."),
    (707, "Endocrine Pancreas: Islet Architecture & Reciprocal Glucose Regulation", "Beta-cells: GLUT2 glucose uptake, ATP generation, ATP-sensitive K+ channel closure, depolarizing Ca2+ influx triggering insulin exocytosis; alpha-cell glucagon; delta-cell somatostatin inhibition."),
    (708, "Cardiac Conduction System & Pacemaker Action Potential Electrophysiology", "SA node spontaneous phase 4 diastolic depolarization mediated by hyperpolarization-activated cyclic nucleotide-gated (HCN) funny current (If), AV node conduction delay, Purkinje fast conduction."),
    (709, "Cardiac Hemodynamics: Pressure-Volume Loops & Frank-Starling Law", "End-diastolic volume (EDV) increasing myocardial sarcomere stretch and cross-bridge sensitivity; stroke volume (SV = EDV - ESV), ejection fraction, inotropic contractility vs afterload shifts on PV loops."),
    (710, "Vascular Hemodynamics: Systemic Vascular Resistance & Arterial Compliance", "Poiseuille resistance equation (R proportional to 1/r^4), arterioles as primary site of peripheral resistance, windkessel effect of elastic aorta dampening systolic pressure swings."),
    (711, "Microcirculatory Fluid Dynamics: Starling Forces & Capillary Exchange", "Capillary hydrostatic pressure (Pc) vs interstitial hydrostatic pressure (Pi); capillary oncotic pressure (pic) vs interstitial oncotic pressure (pii); lymphatic drainage preventing peripheral interstitial edema."),
    (712, "Erythrocyte Physiology, Erythropoiesis & Carbon Dioxide Transport", "Renal peritubular interstitial oxygen sensing, erythropoietin (EPO) stimulation, carbaminohemoglobin formation, chloride shift (Hamburger phenomenon) mediated by Band 3 (AE1) anion exchanger."),
    (713, "Hemostasis & Blood Coagulation: Primary vs Secondary Hemostasis", "Endothelial vWF binding platelet GP Ib, thromboxane A2 and ADP activation; extrinsic tissue factor-FVIIa complex, intrinsic FXII/XI/IX cascade, common pathway FXa converting prothrombin to thrombin."),
    (714, "Lymphatic System Architecture: Fluid Balance, Lipid Transport & Immunity", "Blind-ended initial lymphatic capillaries with overlapping endothelial microvalves, thoracic duct returning chyle and lymph to left subclavian vein, lacteals transporting dietary chylomicrons."),
